  "preamble": "Fortition of the voiceless labiodental fricative [f] to the voiceless bilabial stop [p]. In the Pohnpeic languages of Micronesia, Proto-Micronesian *f regularly became p (*faa- 'four' > Pohnpeian pah, Mokilese pahw), while Kiribati lost it.",
